    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d112">

                <pb facs="0214" n="194" xml:id="pg194"/>

                <head>No. 4.</head>
                <p>I hereby declare that I have this day examined personally the report at the
                    custom-house of the arrival in this port on the 19th September 1863, of the
                    coasting steamer Kadie (in the year 1863.) It states as follows: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>From Cape Town to this port and back to Cape Town, having on board to be
                            shipped to the Alabama: 180 tons coal, 7 barrels pork, 12 cwt. 2 qrs. 0
                            lbs., 5 barrels rum, 287 gallons, 3 bales merchandise.</p>
                        <p>Signed by collector of customs.</p>
                        <p rendition="#right">G. W. BROWNING.</p>
                        <p>Signed and certified as a true report by the master of Kadie.</p>
                        <p rendition="#right">JAMES FOWLER.</p>
                        <p rendition="#right"><seg type="margin">[737]</seg> *J. W. WHITE.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName>Simons Town, Cape of Good
                            Hope</placeName>, sworn before me <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1871-11-02">this 2d November, 1871</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>P. W. MARTIN,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Justice of the
                        Peace.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
